# Website and README

README is the GitHub **and** PyPI long description: what pyiv is, honest install, short quick start, link to https://rl337.org/pyiv/. Do not duplicate the API reference.

**docs/** is the product site. Key Features: type-based injection, scopes, keys/binder, reflection, test doubles, zero dependencies (core). Do not headline Factory. `pyiv-common` is a second package (PyYAML, requests), not a core runtime dep.

**agent-skills/** is customer-facing agent guidance (not maintainer `.cursor/skills/`). Keep it accurate when public APIs or doubles change; document install/links on `docs/guide/agent-skills.rst`.

Install must match README and release notes: `pip install pyiv`. Related: `pip install pyiv-common`. Unreleased `main` may use `pip install git+https://github.com/rl337/pyiv.git`. No Poetry.

API nav: grouped `toctree`s on `docs/index.rst` (User guide, Core DI, Bindings, Discovery, Test doubles, Integrations, Related packages). User guide pages live in `docs/guide/` with human titles. Keep `collapse_navigation: False` and `titles_only: True`. Omit `binder_impl`. New public core modules need `docs/pyiv/pyiv.<name>.rst` and a toctree entry.

Production is https://rl337.org/pyiv/ from `main`. PR previews are `/branch/<branch>/` only.

If a changelog page exists, link it from the site (homepage + Reference toctree) and from `project.urls`. `CHANGELOG.md` is the source of truth; `docs/changelog.rst` includes it.
